                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "Nun (נ) is the **14th letter** of the Hebrew alphabet , carrying a numerical value (gematria) of **50** and the sound of **\"n\"** (as in \"noon\").[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Nun/nun.html)[[2]](https://www.facebook.com/100068612731591/posts/how-to-write-the-hebrew-letter-nun-in-blockscriptnun-%D7%A0-final-nun-%D7%9F-alphabetical-/851145567182527/)\n\n### Key Forms\n\n- **Medial/Initial Form (נ):** A bent shape called *nun kefufah* , representing humility and bowing.\n- **Final Form (ן):** A straight, elongated shape called *nun sofit* or *nun peshutah* , used when the letter appears at the end of a word.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137086/jewish/Nun.htm)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MynXTRENj70&t=6)[[3]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nun_(letter))[[4]](https://www.facebook.com/100068612731591/posts/how-to-write-the-hebrew-letter-nun-in-blockscriptnun-%D7%A0-final-nun-%D7%9F-alphabetical-/851145567182527/)\n\n### Meaning & Symbolism\n\n- **Fish & Life:** *Nun* means \"fish\" in Aramaic, symbolizing fertility, movement, and life.\n- **Faithfulness:** It is the first letter of *ne'eman* (faithful) and represents a humble servant before God.\n- **The Dreidel:** On the Hanukkah spinning top (*sivivon*), *Nun* stands for the word *nes* (miracle), part of the phrase \"A great miracle happened there\".\n- **Gematria 50:** Represents the **50 Gates of Understanding** (*Binah* ) and the **Jubilee year** (the 50th year of freedom).[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GTAva-z1jfM&t=1)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Nun/nun.html)[[3]](https://dinahoverlien.com/2020/07/08/nun/)[[4]](https://www.facebook.com/100068612731591/posts/how-to-write-the-hebrew-letter-nun-in-blockscriptnun-%D7%A0-final-nun-%D7%9F-alphabetical-/851145567182527/)[[5]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MynXTRENj70&t=6)[[6]](https://kriakala.com/hebrew-letter-nun)[[7]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137086/jewish/Nun.htm)\n\nLearn more about its structure and history on [Chabad.org](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137086/jewish/Nun.htm) or read the detailed overview on [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nun_(letter)).Would you like to know how *Nun* is used in specific Hebrew words, or explore the meaning of other letters in the alphabet?",
